  "worked_solution": "The global extrema of a function are the lowest or highest points of the function's graph over its entire domain.\n\nThe lowest point is the global minimum, whereas the highest point is the global maximum.\n\nAccording to the graph, the highest points are $B$ and $D$, and so these points represents the global maximum of $f(x).$",
